msgid "挂载命名空间快照"
msgstr "Mount namespace snapshots"

msgid ""
"``vfs_namespace_snapshot()`` 在独占 VFS 执行权下，将活动挂载树复制到地址固定、 "
"由调用方管理的空命名空间中。它保留覆盖层、不可绑定挂载和图内传播关系；新旧 "
"命名空间之间不会建立传播关系。各副本直接持有原生文件系统后端，共享目录项和 文件内容，但挂载策略和写入者计数独立。挂载 ID 从 VFS "
"全局序列分配，传播组号 仍仅在各自的命名空间内有意义。"
msgstr ""
"With exclusive VFS execution ownership, ``vfs_namespace_snapshot()`` "
"copies an active mount tree into an empty namespace at a stable address "
"owned by the caller. It preserves overmounts, unbindable mounts, and "
"propagation relationships within the graph. There is no propagation "
"between the original and copied namespaces. Each copy directly pins the "
"native filesystem backend and shares dentries and file contents, but "
"keeps its own mount policy and writer count. The VFS assigns mount IDs "
"from a global sequence; propagation group IDs remain namespace-local."

msgid ""
"可选的 root 和 cwd 引用按原挂载对象和目录项重新绑定，而不是重新查找路径； "
"即使路径已被其他挂载覆盖，所指目录项也不变。已摘除的路径保持原样，其他活动 命名空间的路径返回 "
"``EXDEV``。所有分配完成后才发布新树并替换路径；失败时 不改变原树、目标、路径或 ID 游标。"
msgstr ""
"Optional root and cwd references are rebound by original attachment and "
"dentry identity, not by looking up the pathname again. An overmount does "
"not change the referenced dentry. Detached paths stay unchanged; a path "
"in another live namespace returns ``EXDEV``. The new tree and path "
"replacements are published only after all allocations succeed. Failure "
"leaves the original tree, destination, paths, and ID cursor unchanged."

msgid ""
"最后一个图使用者离开时，``vfs_namespace_retire()`` 摘除整棵树而不传播卸载。 "
"已持有的路径继续有效，后端由现有的延迟清理队列处理。与之不同，严格的 ``vfs_namespace_destroy()`` "
"在仍有外部引用时拒绝销毁。此接口用于内核内部； 当前没有向用户态开放挂载命名空间创建或切换。"
msgstr ""
"After the last graph user leaves, ``vfs_namespace_retire()`` detaches the"
" entire tree without propagating unmounts. Held paths remain valid and "
"the existing deferred queue handles backend teardown. The stricter "
"``vfs_namespace_destroy()`` instead rejects destruction while external "
"references remain. These are internal kernel interfaces; creation and "
"switching of mount namespaces are not yet exposed to userspace."
